arded by early Turkic peoples as the seat of legitimate rule.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/otumba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otumba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Otumba</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Otumba is a town in the State of Mexico, north-east of Mexico City, close to the ruins of Teotihuacan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ouadane"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouadane.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ouadane</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ouadane is an oasis town in the Adrar region of Mauritania, founded in the 12th century by Berber traders on the edge of the Sahara.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ouaddai-region"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouaddai-region.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ouaddaï Region</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ouaddaï is a province of eastern Chad on the border with Sudan, with its capital at Abéché.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ouahigouya"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouahigouya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ouahigouya</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ouahigouya is a city in northern Burkina Faso and the capital of the North Region.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ouarsenis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouarsenis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ouarsenis</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ouarsenis is a mountain range of the Tell Atlas in north-western 