 has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ouro-preto"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ouro-preto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ouro Preto</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ouro Preto, formerly Vila Rica, is a town in the mountains of Minas Gerais, Brazil, founded during the gold rush of the late 17th and early 18th centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ourthe"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ourthe.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ourthe</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ourthe is a river in the Belgian Ardennes, about 165 kilometres long, which flows north to join the Meuse at Liège.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/outer-mongolia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/outer-mongolia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Outer Mongolia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Outer Mongolia was the northern part of Mongolia under the Qing dynasty, inhabited mainly by the Khalkha Mongols, who submitted to the Kangxi Emperor in 1691.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ovambo-people"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ovambo-people.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ovambo people</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ovambo, or Aawambo, are a Bantu-speaking people of northern Namibia and southern Angola, the largest ethnic group of Namibia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ovamboland"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ovamboland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ovamboland</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ovamboland is the region of northern Namibia inhabited by the Ovambo people, between the Etosha Pan and the Angolan border.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ove-gjedde"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ove-gjedde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ove Gjedde</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ove Gjedde was a Danish naval officer who led the first expedition of the Danish East India Company to Asia, sailing in 1618.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/overgrazing"><span class="enc-name">Overgrazing</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Overgrazing occurs when livestock graze pasture more heavily than it can recover, degrading the land.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ovid"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ovid.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ovid</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ovid was a Roman poet, born at Sulmo in the land of the Paeligni in 43 BCE, the author of the Metamorphoses, the Art of Love and the Fasti, a poem on the Roman calendar…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oviedo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/oviedo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oviedo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Oviedo is the capital of Asturias in northern Spain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ovimbundu"><span class="enc-name">Ovimbundu</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ovimbundu are a Bantu-speaking people of the central highlands of present-day Angola, active as long-distance traders in the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-i